    <h1>Affiliate Marketing for Beginners</h1>

    <p>
      Affiliate marketing is a way to earn commissions by recommending
      products or services from companies that offer affiliate programs.
    </p>

    <h2>How Does It Work?</h2>

    <p>
      You join an affiliate program and receive a special tracking link.
      When someone purchases through your link, you may receive a commission.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 1 — Choose a Topic</h2>

    <p>
      Start with something you understand or want to learn about, such as
      technology, education, fitness, fashion, software, or online tools.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 2 — Find Suitable Products</h2>

    <p>
      Look for legitimate products that provide real value to your audience.
      Always check the terms and conditions of an affiliate program before
      promoting it.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 3 — Create Useful Content</h2>

    <p>
      You can create educational videos, reviews, tutorials, social media
      posts, or articles that genuinely help people.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 4 — Share Your Affiliate Link</h2>

    <p>
      Where permitted by the platform and affiliate program, you can share
      your affiliate link with your audience. Be transparent that you may
      earn a commission from qualifying purchases.
    </p>

    <h2>Important Tip</h2>

    <p>
      Affiliate marketing is not guaranteed income. Focus on helping people,
      building trust, and learning consistently rather than promising quick
      money.
    </p>

